{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: correct the record guide's description of which code admits events and runs the fold. Queue after your existing work through #21356; keep all earlier queue positions and full Tailapp I7 intact.\n\nThe [guide](docs/concepts/record.md@3ecb8b77d55cfe8ccb1d634649788a4ab629577b:64) says the newest ratified admission-profile governance statement chooses the rules a workroom runs. That describes a library selection model as an active submission switch. The [actual submitter](internal/app/app.go@3ecb8b77d55cfe8ccb1d634649788a4ab629577b:2284) installs the application's allowlist and admission hooks; [admitApplication](internal/app/admission.go@3ecb8b77d55cfe8ccb1d634649788a4ab629577b:316) evaluates new submissions against the verified pre-sequence world. [Interpreter selection](internal/app/host.go@3ecb8b77d55cfe8ccb1d634649788a4ab629577b:93) is fixed when a workspace opens from its supported host binding.\n\nI reproduced the distinction through the real Act/AcceptSubmission path in a disposable test workroom: a ratified governance record named an unavailable contract, the library resolver selected it, and the next assertion still appended effectively under the unchanged installed interpreter. [Probe evidence](admission-profile-probe.json) and [probe source](admission-profile-probe_test.go) are attached. This is a documentation mismatch, not an admitted-security-exploit claim. Historical #739 commissioned the governance/selection library; the [deployment note](notes/2026-08-07-deployment.md@3ecb8b77d55cfe8ccb1d634649788a4ab629577b:1537) explicitly distinguishes it from downstream machinery that remains unimplemented. Do not reopen #739 or implement a new admission-profile runtime to make the prose true.\n\nDeliver a small documentation correction in request/record-guide-admission-clarity:\n\n1. Replace the misleading admission paragraph with a concise account of the shipped boundaries: installed application guards govern submission; admission-profile records and their library selector do not replace those guards or load a bundle. Distinguish host binding/interpreter availability from workroom governance records. Explain only what a reader needs, linking maintained architecture detail where useful.\n2. In the adjacent fold paragraph, distinguish the deterministic fold library from the resident and CLI that actually invoke it. Remove the blanket claim that gitseq never runs a fold on the reader's behalf. Preserve independent replay and recorded-versus-effective acts.\n3. Rest the corrected page on current implementation artifacts for the behavior it describes. Reconcile each cited owner and the current host-binding contract; preserve ordinary staleness honestly. The attached current-basis check selects incorporated revisions whose relevant file bytes match examined main. Do not retire unrelated wider or foreign candidates.\n4. Verify the exact prose against source and the attached behavioral counterexample. Use existing focused host-binding/admission tests plus the documented documentation gates, links and owning-head file previews. A new permanent wording-only test is unnecessary. If retaining a behavioral regression, make it prove the boundary rather than repeat a sentence. Obtain independent Architecture/Security/Simplification review, ratify it, seal the approved head to main with exact-path succession, push, check required CI and remove the owned branch/worktree.\n\nScope is docs/concepts/record.md and only a directly necessary supporting reference correction found during this check. No runtime, governance-kind, authority, schema, dependency, public API, reader deployment, historical cleanup or broad documentation rewrite. This repairs current prose discovered during the #3029 migration audit; it does not declare every original migration condition complete. #21309 separately owns the event-ID page update and its source-basis finding already sent in chat.","body":{"branch":"request/record-guide-admission-clarity","conditions":"Correct the record guide admission-profile and fold-execution claims to match shipped application/host behavior; reconcile behavior bases; verify focused evidence and documentation; independently review, seal/push main, verify CI and clean up. No runtime or governance change.","head":"3ecb8b77d55cfe8ccb1d634649788a4ab629577b","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:4febdd933de14fb3b72d711a585e4c04043a1306, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:8a60f7689221433c1d85948c2bbe7c3cd6258388, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a0c1f08bff46a3ce1e4cfca5ef4b108a72405bf4 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:00925ae6c09fb0b8e2a72e84c22ca3488bc9534d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:012451209d3000492d2e523089e5973beec05f61, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:015aba51ab6c2416861618c5ac3c9ae0e444f17f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:069ba281df08c36e7b19c66532ae24357887a9e5 and 109 more","target_head":"3ecb8b77d55cfe8ccb1d634649788a4ab629577b","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}